{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.QzBicompletion","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.QzBicompletion","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Eval.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HabiroRing.projectToZHabiro","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HabiroRing.projectToZHabiro","kind":"def","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/qz-bicompletion.lean#L77-L83","doc":"Projection to the z-only Habiro ring by specialising q ↦ q_0 and\nforgetting the m-grading. The resulting element is determined by\nits n-family of polynomials evaluated at q = q_0. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HabiroRing.projectToQHabiro","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HabiroRing.projectToQHabiro","kind":"def","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/qz-bicompletion.lean#L69-L75","doc":"Projection to the q-only Habiro ring by setting z ↦ 0 and\nforgetting the n-grading. The resulting element is determined by\nits m-family of constant polynomials in z. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HabiroRing.QZBicompletionElement.compatible_n","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HabiroRing.QZBicompletionElement.compatible_n","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/qz-bicompletion.lean#L66-L66","doc":"Compatibility under increment of n (cyclotomic step in z). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HabiroRing.QZBicompletionElement.compatible_m","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HabiroRing.QZBicompletionElement.compatible_m","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/qz-bicompletion.lean#L63-L63","doc":"Compatibility under increment of m (cyclotomic step in q). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HabiroRing.QZBicompletionElement.family","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HabiroRing.QZBicompletionElement.family","kind":"def","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/qz-bicompletion.lean#L61-L61","doc":"Polynomial representative at each (m, n) level. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HabiroRing.QZBicompletionElement.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HabiroRing.QZBicompletionElement.mk","kind":"ctor","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/qz-bicompletion.lean#L59-L59","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HabiroRing.QZBicompletionElement","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HabiroRing.QZBicompletionElement","kind":"structure","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/qz-bicompletion.lean#L55-L67","doc":"The (q, z)-bicompletion as a doubly-indexed compatible family of\npolynomial representatives. Mirrors `ZHabiroElement` but with two\ncyclotomic levels (m for q, n for z) instead of one. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:qz-bicompletion","label":"def:qz-bicompletion","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/qz-bicompletion.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HabiroRing.QZBicompletionEquiv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HabiroRing.QZBicompletionEquiv","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/qz-bicompletion.lean#L49-L53","doc":"Equivalence relation at level (m, n): f ≡ g (mod I_{m,n}) iff\n(f - g) lies in the ideal generated by I_{m,n}(q, ·). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HabiroRing.qzBigradedIdealGen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HabiroRing.qzBigradedIdealGen","kind":"def","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/qz-bicompletion.lean#L44-L47","doc":"The bigraded ideal generator I_{m,n}(q, z) = (q;q)_m · P_n(q, z).\nReturned as a polynomial in z whose coefficients depend on q. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HabiroRing.zPochhammer","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HabiroRing.zPochhammer","kind":"def","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/qz-bicompletion.lean#L33-L42","doc":"The z-Pochhammer polynomial P_n(q, z) = ∏_{k=1}^{n}(1 - q^{-k} z), as a\npolynomial in z with real coefficients depending on q.  Identical to the\ncanonical definition in the sibling `z-habiro-ring.lean` (same namespace);\nredeclared here because content-block siblings cannot import one another\n(the same reason `qPochhammerProduct` above is a local copy).  Added\n2026-09-05: the file referred to `zPochhammer` without any definition in\ntracked history, and did not compile. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HabiroRing.qPochhammerProduct","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HabiroRing.qPochhammerProduct","kind":"def","line":27,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/qz-bicompletion.lean#L27-L31","doc":"The q-Pochhammer (q;q)_m = ∏_{k=1}^{m}(1 - q^k), reused from\n`habiro-ring.lean`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}